From 5d1417ca8bd96430883bb53b1e2fdb68917b8e1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Publish only the site: a Pages job deploys the SITE list,
 the e2e serves it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GitHub Pages used to serve the whole branch, so src/, the tests, the
notes and the tooling were all online. Now:

- src/build.js exports SITE — index.html, 404.html, slides/, engine/,
  resources/, transcripts/ — the index pages, the built decks and
  everything they load at runtime, and nothing else; `bun build.js --site`
  copies exactly that list to _site/ (`make site`, after `make check`)
- verify.yml gains a `pages` job: on a push to master, once `verify`
  passed, `make site` + actions/upload-pages-artifact + deploy-pages
  (permissions pages: write + id-token: write, one deploy at a time).
  One-time setup on the repo: Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions
- the e2e server serves only SITE (plus its own fixtures): a deck that
  reaches for anything outside the published set gets a 404 in the tests,
  which decks.test.js already fails on, instead of online. All 11 e2e
  tests still pass, which shows the decks reference only the six entries
- a new top-level directory the decks need (audio/, say) goes into SITE;
  README's Publishing section says so

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
