+## Publishing
+GitHub Pages publishes ONLY the site: the `pages` job of
+[verify.yml](.github/workflows/verify.yml) runs `make site` (= copies the
+`SITE` list of `src/build.js` to `_site/`) and deploys that, on every push to
+`master` once `verify` passed — `src/`, the notes and the tooling never go
+online. The e2e server serves the same list, so a deck that reaches outside
+it fails the tests before it 404s online; a new top-level directory the decks
+need (`audio/`, say) goes into `SITE`. One-time setup on the repo: Settings →
+Pages → Build and deployment → Source: **GitHub Actions**.
